  "paragraph": "The census asks whether the store's series IS Close (as_traded), IS a constant multiple of Adj Close (dividend_adjusted), or is a partial mixture of the two (mixed: between 0.20 and 0.80 of days on either). The store series for these nine is none of them: it is within 0.5 percent of Close on only 3 to 9 percent of days, within 0.5 percent of Adj Close on 0 to 10 percent, and its ratio to Adj Close is not constant (share_ra_c 0.09 to 0.35 for eight funds; CPXIX 0.7876, the nearest, 0.0124 under the 0.80 bar). Round 71 measured the store's adjustment as larger than Yahoo's own Adj Close (slope 1.0 to 4.2), which is consistent with share_adj staying under 0.10, below the 0.20 mixed floor. Each therefore fell to other:matches_neither, a class as_traded_store does not substitute. The change that would have substituted them is to add class other (at least its matches_neither reason) to SUBSTITUTE_CLASSES; this cell does not make it. The census was not re-run (it fetches); its committed csv was read."
